+# T60 Result
+
+## Files created/modified
+
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/consolidate_session.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_memory_metrics.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_event_trace.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/admin_tools_tests.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/mod.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/event_capture.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mod.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/reader.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/mod.rs`
+- `README.md`
+
+## Verification commands and outputs
+
+1. `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/consolidate_session.rs`
+   - Result: `ok`
+
+2. `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_event_trace.rs`
+   - Result: `ok`
+
+3. `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_memory_metrics.rs`
+   - Result: `ok`
+
+4. `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/admin_tools_tests.rs`
+   - Result: `ok`
+
+5. `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::memory_v2::admin_tools_tests`
+   - Result: passed
+   - Output summary:
+     - `running 4 tests`
+     - `serde_round_trips_admin_tool_requests_and_responses ... ok`
+     - `get_memory_metrics_returns_every_required_signal_or_honest_null ... ok`
+     - `get_event_trace_enforces_workspace_boundary_and_has_stable_pagination ... ok`
+     - `consolidate_session_emits_proposals_without_direct_writes_and_proposals_are_actionable ... ok`
+     - `test result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 85 filtered out`
+
+## Issues encountered
+
+- The existing `memory_v2` surface was only partially integrated into the RPC crate. `rpc/mod.rs` was missing the `memory_v2` module export, and the new T60 tools were not registered in the MCP tool list or dispatcher.
+- The existing `propose_memory_evolution(action=apply|reject)` path bypassed the canonical consolidation proposal apply/reject flow and would not correctly materialize T60 consolidation proposals. I replaced that path with the real `ConsolidationProposal::apply` / `reject` flow so T60 proposals are auditable and actionable through the required tool.
+- `get_event_trace` needed stable pagination support from the event reader, so I added a bounded `EventReader::execute_page` API instead of doing ad hoc scans in the RPC layer.
+- The daemon test target still emits pre-existing warnings in unrelated memory-v2 test files. They did not block T60 verification.
+
+## Final status
+
+complete

 succeeded in 108ms:
codex
Implemented T60 end to end. The new MCP tools are wired into the daemon surface: `consolidate_session`, `get_memory_metrics`, and `get_event_trace`, with bounded event-trace pagination, proposal-only session consolidation, fallback Phase 9 metric reporting, and admin-tool coverage in [admin_tools_tests.rs](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/admin_tools_tests.rs). I also fixed the existing `propose_memory_evolution(action=apply|reject)` path so consolidation proposals are actually applied through the canonical proposal flow instead of a partial direct-write shortcut.

Verification ran with the exact T60 commands: both required files exist, and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::memory_v2::admin_tools_tests` passed with 4/4 tests. The required result artifact is written at [T60.md](/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/results/T60.md). Residual warnings remain in unrelated existing memory-v2 test files, but they did not block T60 verification.
